ok    R30 arm A guest     = the isolate's 65536-byte ring object at 0x0000000120020000 (semaphore 0x0000000120022000) is UNCLAIMED in the guest-bound space — a fresh object took the address and RM reported it back
ok    R30 arm B control   = the SAME call REFUSES at 0x0000000120020000 in the control space (NoMemory) — the probe can detect occupancy, so arm A's `Free` is a measurement and not a constant
★     R30 arm C REFUSED   = the guest-bound engine did NOT retire a read of 0x0000000120022000 (sem 0x00000000, GP_GET 2 GP_PUT 2) — the address does not resolve in the space a guest channel is bound to. ⚠ Expect one `Xid 31 FAULT_PDE` in the host dmesg for this channel; that is the boundary, not a bug
★     R30 executor VAS    = the isolate's CE semaphore is NOT nameable from the address space a guest channel is bound to
done — executor-VAS probe only
